  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 22,
    "summary": "Eliphaz accuses Job of various sins and exhorts him to repent.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Can a man be profitable unto God, as he that is wise may be profitable unto himself?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Is it any pleasure to the Almighty, that thou art righteous? or is it gain to him, that thou makest thy ways perfect?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "Mosiah 2:21 (20–22)."
          },
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "2 Sam. 22:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 69
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Sam. 22:33.",
            "prettyString": "2 Samuel 22:33",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 22,
                    "end": 22,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 33,
                        "end": 33
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Will he reprove thee for fear of thee? will he enter with thee into judgment?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Is not thy wickedness great? and thine iniquities infinite?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "For thou hast taken a pledge from thy brother for nought, and stripped the naked of their clothing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou hast not given water to the weary to drink, and thou hast withholden bread from the hungry.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Bread."
          },
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "Matt. 25:42; Mosiah 4:26; Alma 4:12 (12–13)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Bread.",
            "prettyString": "TG Bread",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Bread",
                "entryId": "tg-bread",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "But as for the mighty man, he had the earth; and the honourable man dwelt in it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou hast sent widows away empty, and the arms of the fatherless have been broken.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "Job 31:21 (21–22); James 1:27; 3 Ne. 24:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore snares are round about thee, and sudden fear troubleth thee;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Or darkness, that thou canst not see; and abundance of waters cover thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 17
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Is not God in the height of heaven? and behold the height of the stars, how high they are!",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And thou sayest, How doth God know? can he judge through the dark cloud?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "Ps. 73:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Ps. 94:9 (7–10); D&C 88:41."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 73:11.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 73:11",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 73,
                    "end": 73,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 11,
                        "end": 11
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Thick clouds are a covering to him, that he seeth not; and he walketh in the circuit of heaven.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Hast thou marked the old way which wicked men have trodden?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Which were cut down out of time, whose foundation was overflown with a flood:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Which said unto God, Depart from us: and what can the Almighty do for them?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet he filled their houses with good things: but the counsel of the wicked is far from me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "The righteous see it, and are glad: and the innocent laugh them to scorn.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Whereas our substance is not cut down, but the remnant of them the fire consumeth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Acquaint now thyself with him, and be at peace: thereby good shall come unto thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "IE God."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "TG Peace of God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Peace of God.",
            "prettyString": "TG Peace of God",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Peace of God",
                "entryId": "tg-peace-of-god",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Receive, I pray thee, the law from his mouth, and lay up his words in thine heart.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 22:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou return to the Almighty, thou shalt be built up, thou shalt put away iniquity far from thy tabernacles.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "1 Ne. 17:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Ne. 17:3.",
            "prettyString": "1 Nephi 17:3",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1nephi",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 17,
